From 2edb6fd9209f20f000493645df343a09764af90e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Enrique Magallon <dev.ace.93.03@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 18:38:38 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Continuous touchpad swipe between workspaces in the
 overview

cosmic-comp already forwards 3+ finger swipes to the overview's layer
surface (zwp_pointer_gestures_v1) while it is open, but nothing listened.
Bind pointer gestures on the wayland thread (same client as iced), track
the swipe like cosmic-comp's workspace gesture, and show the neighbouring
workspaces in a strip that follows the fingers, then settles with a
spring that keeps the release velocity.

Neighbouring workspaces' toplevels are captured while the overview is
open so they are ready when a swipe starts.
